[al:新概念英语第一册]
[ti:129. Seventy Miles an Hour]
[00:00.740]Lesson 129 | 第129课
[00:03.855]Look, Harry! | 看，哈里！
[00:06.560]That policeman's waving to you. | 那个警察在向你招手。
[00:09.725]He wants you to stop. | 他想让你停车。
[00:12.415]Where do you think you are? | 你以为你在哪里？
[00:15.740]On a racetrack? | 在赛车道上吗？
[00:17.950]You must have been driving at 70 miles an hour. | 你一定是以每小时70英里的速度行驶。
[00:22.495]I can't have been. | 我不可能开那么快。
[00:24.615]I was doing 80 when I overtook you. | 我超车时，我开到了80英里每小时。
[00:29.680]Didn't you see the speed limit? | 你没看到限速标志吗？
[00:33.290]I'm afraid I didn't, officer. | 恐怕我没有，警官。
[00:36.085]I must have been dreaming. | 我一定是做梦了。
[00:38.290]He wasn't dreaming, officer. I was telling him to drive slowly. | 他没做梦，警官。我当时正叫他开慢点。
[00:44.385]That's why I didn't see the sign. | 所以我才没看到牌子。
[00:47.890]Let me see your driving license and your insurance certificate. | 让我看看你的驾驶执照和保险凭证。
[00:54.655]I won't charge you this time, but you'd better not do it again. | 这次我不罚你，但你最好别再犯了。
[01:01.620]Thank you. | 谢谢你。
[01:03.650]I'll certainly be more careful. | 我一定会更小心。
[01:07.300]I told you to drive slowly, Harry. | 我叫你开慢点，哈里。
[01:11.850]You always tell me to drive slowly, dear. | 你总是叫我开慢点，亲爱的。
[01:15.585]Well, next time you'd better take my advice. | 好吧，下次你最好听我的建议。